── `when` IN A LAZY VALUE'S FUNCTION ── E0435_when_in_a_lazy_values_function.lt:7:20  [E0435]

A `Lazy`'s function must not wait, but this `when` holds shared values; read
them before `Lazy.new`:

  7 │   lazy.Lazy.new(|| when rates { amount * rates.euro })
    │                 ───────────────────────────────────── `Lazy.new` computes its value with this function
    │                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

A `Lazy` computes its value whenever it is first asked for, so its function must
not wait for shared values. Read them before, and capture the copy.
